@startuml

salt
{
  <b>ORE STUDIO - REPORTING: RESULTS BY COUNTERPARTY</b>
  --
  <b>RUN: Cross-Entity Counterparty Concentration - 4b7e1a02</b>
  --
  {#
    Party | Runs | State | Took
    ACMCOR | npv, saccr | completed | 2 m 18 s
  }
  --
  <b>THE COUNTERPARTIES THIS RUN IS EXPOSED TO</b>
  --
  {#
    Code | Counterparty | NPV USD m | Notional USD m | Trades | Exposure USD m | Share
    . | <b>MERIDIAN CAPITAL GROUP</b> | 12.5 | 2,418.0 | 1,742 | 918.4 | 14.1%
    MERID | Meridian Capital | 8.2 | 1,610.0 | 1,204 | 604.3 | 9.3%
    MERID-UK | Meridian Capital UK | 4.3 | 808.0 | 538 | 314.2 | 4.8%
    . | <b>ACME BANK PLC</b> | 21.9 | 3,902.0 | 2,318 | 1,486.3 | 24.8%
    ACMEBK | ACME Bank PLC | 21.9 | 3,902.0 | 2,318 | 1,486.3 | 24.8%
    NRTHCLR | NORTHGATE CLEARING | 9.1 | 1,744.0 | 906 | 512.9 | 10.3%
    HANSAPF | HANSA PFANDBRIEF | 2.9 | 622.0 | 214 | 88.7 | 3.3%
    PACTRST | PACIFIC TRUST | 1.7 | 418.0 | 168 | 41.2 | 1.9%
    KSTLASR | KESTREL ASSURANCE | 0.9 | 212.0 | 96 | 18.4 | 1.0%
    . | <b>Total, largest first</b> | 88.4 | 18,204.0 | 18,204 | 3,248.5 | 100%
  }
  Largest first, by exposure where the report runs =saccr= and by aggregate NPV
  where it does not. A group row sits above its members and carries the sum of
  them; a member keeps its own figure because the desk faces the member and
  credit faces the group. No operation returns a result grouped by counterparty,
  and nothing parses the archive, so every figure here is a fixture.
  --
  <b>ONE COUNTERPARTY: ACME BANK PLC (ACMEBK)</b>
  --
  {#
    Netting Set | Trades | NPV USD m | Exposure USD m | Errors
    ACME-CSA-1 | 1,842 | 17.2 | 1,180.4 | 0
    ACME-CSA-2 | 476 | 4.7 | 305.9 | 2
  }
  {#
    Trade | Type | Notional USD m | NPV | Netting Set | Error
    2df8fa31... | Swap | 40.0 | 1.28 | CSA-1 | -
    2d0f8a31... | Bond | 40.0 | - | CSA-2 | Analytics
  }
  The trade is the trading trade with that id, and the trade names its
  counterparty_id. The error scopes are Trade, Analytics, Curve, Configuration
  and Report: none of them is a counterparty, so a counterparty's errors are
  reached through the trades that name it, and an error recorded against the
  analytic alone is not divided across names.
  --
  <b>A COUNTERPARTY WITH NO RESULT</b>
  --
  {#
    Code | Counterparty | NPV | Notional | Trades | Exposure | Share
    BLUERIV | BLUE RIVER PENSION | - | - | 0 | - | -
  }
  The party can see this counterparty and the run produced nothing for it. It is
  listed, not dropped, and it is not a measure of zero.
  --
  <b>A TRADE THAT NAMES NO COUNTERPARTY</b>
  --
  {#
    Heading | Trades | Notional USD m | NPV USD m
    counterparty_scope = intra_entity | 412 | 980.0 | 1.2
  }
  The schema allows counterparty_id to be null when the scope is intra_entity. The
  run's counterparty totals are less than the run's total by this amount, and the
  screen says so rather than folding it into a name.
}

@enduml
